    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "Find integers $p$ and $q$ such that $\\dfrac{\\sqrt5}{\\sqrt5-2}=p+q\\sqrt5$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$p=5,\\ q=2$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\sqrt5}{\\sqrt5-2}&=\\frac{\\sqrt5(\\sqrt5+2)}{(\\sqrt5-2)(\\sqrt5+2)}\\\\\\frac{\\sqrt5}{\\sqrt5-2}&=\\frac{5+2\\sqrt5}{5-4}\\\\\\frac{\\sqrt5}{\\sqrt5-2}&=5+2\\sqrt5\\end{align*}$$\n\nComparing with $p+q\\sqrt5$ gives $p=5$ and $q=2$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
